Well, Death Quaker showed me that this still isn't exactly a very
risk-proof
method. It is risky, but I still plan to do it with a few more
precautions
in the future.

When you hit "q" on a sink, you can drink from it. Just like a
fountain.

Randomly, a random potion comes out. Of course, a water elemental
may come out, or a sewer rat. Be sure you can handle them. A random
ring may come out also, but this happens rarely and only once per sink.

And you can also gain a single exp point from quaffing. And finally,
polymorph
may come out and you will be transformed for a while.

When a random potion comes out, you get a chance to identify it.

If something happens like... a red liquid flows out of the sink. It
burns!
Name the liquid acid, and whenever you come across red liquid in the
future, it will be called acid instead.

